-- ccc17-dna-orders.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, sections 487.05 to 487.0552: the DNA warrant, the DNA orders
-- and authorizations, appeals, the offenders-serving-sentences authorization, failure to appear and failure to comply.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Source: the plain-text rendering (made by a converter script) of the Justice Laws Website consolidation
-- (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- Every name begins with the label of the provision it implements. Every function answers MAYBE BOOLEAN (or a MAYBE of a type of this
-- module): JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words, NOTHING everywhere else (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result").
-- Seam inputs (answers computed by another part, taken as inputs): `s 487.04 ...` (ccc16).

§ `Section 487.05 -- Information for warrant to take bodily substances for forensic DNA analysis`

DECLARE `s 487.05(1)(b) place where the bodily substance was found or obtained` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.05(1)(b)(i) at the place where the offence was committed`
    `s 487.05(1)(b)(ii) on or within the body of the victim of the offence`
    `s 487.05(1)(b)(iii) on anything worn or carried by the victim at the time when the offence was committed`
    `s 487.05(1)(b)(iv) on or within the body of any person or thing or at any place associated with the commission of the offence`
    `s 487.05(1)(b) somewhere else`

-- covers: 487.05(1)
-- fork: F1
-- jural: a provincial court judge > the person from whom samples would be taken > power
-- src:9545 | 487.05 (1) A provincial court judge who on ex parte application made in Form 5.01 is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe
-- src:9546 | (a) that a designated offence has been committed,
-- src:9547 | (b) that a bodily substance has been found or obtained
-- src:9548 | (i) at the place where the offence was committed,
-- src:9549 | (ii) on or within the body of the victim of the offence,
-- src:9550 | (iii) on anything worn or carried by the victim at the time when the offence was committed, or
-- src:9551 | (iv) on or within the body of any person or thing or at any place associated with the commission of the offence,
-- src:9552 | (c) that a person was a party to the offence, and
-- src:9553 | (d) that forensic DNA analysis of a bodily substance from the person will provide evidence about whether the bodily substance referred to in paragraph (b) was from that person
-- src:9554 | and who is satisfied that it is in the best interests of the administration of justice to do so may issue a warrant in Form 5.02 authorizing the taking, from that person, for the purpose of forensic DNA analysis, of any number of samples of one or more bodily substances that is reasonably required for that purpose, by means of the investigative procedures described in subsection 487.06(1).
@ref s 487.05(1) (src:9545-9554)
-- A provincial court judge MAY issue a DNA warrant (Form 5.02) when each of limbs (a) to (d), the oath, the ex parte application and the best-interests
-- satisfaction is met. A grant gated by "who ... is satisfied": a failed gate answers NOTHING, not JUST FALSE (ruling of 2026-11-12, limit (1); fork F1).
GIVEN `the application is made to a provincial court judge ex parte in Form 5.01` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied by information on oath` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 487.04 the offence is a designated offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds to believe that the designated offence has been committed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `where the bodily substance was found or obtained` IS A `s 487.05(1)(b) place where the bodily substance was found or obtained`
      `there are reasonable grounds to believe that the bodily substance has been found or obtained there` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds to believe that the person was a party to the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds to believe that forensic DNA analysis of a bodily substance from the person will provide evidence about whether the bodily substance found was from that person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that it is in the best interests of the administration of justice to issue the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.05(1) the provincial court judge may issue a warrant in Form 5.02` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the application is made to a provincial court judge ex parte in Form 5.01` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF NOT `the judge is satisfied by information on oath` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF NOT (`s 487.04 the offence is a designated offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text)
        IF NOT `there are reasonable grounds to believe that the designated offence has been committed` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `where the bodily substance was found or obtained` EQUALS `s 487.05(1)(b) somewhere else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF NOT `there are reasonable grounds to believe that the bodily substance has been found or obtained there` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF NOT `there are reasonable grounds to believe that the person was a party to the offence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF NOT `there are reasonable grounds to believe that forensic DNA analysis of a bodily substance from the person will provide evidence about whether the bodily substance found was from that person` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF NOT `the judge is satisfied that it is in the best interests of the administration of justice to issue the warrant` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 487.05(2) matter the judge considers` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.05(2)(a) the nature of the designated offence and the circumstances of its commission`
    `s 487.05(2)(b)(i) whether there is a peace officer who is able, by virtue of training or experience, to take samples of bodily substances from the person`
    `s 487.05(2)(b)(ii) whether there is another person who is able, by virtue of training or experience, to take samples under the direction of a peace officer`
    `s 487.05(2) another matter`

-- covers: 487.05(2)
-- jural: the person from whom samples would be taken > a provincial court judge > right
-- src:9556 | (2) In considering whether to issue the warrant, the provincial court judge shall have regard to all relevant matters, including
-- src:9557 | (a) the nature of the designated offence and the circumstances of its commission; and
-- src:9558 | (b) whether there is
-- src:9559 | (i) a peace officer who is able, by virtue of training or experience, to take samples of bodily substances from the person, by means of the investigative procedures described in subsection 487.06(1), or
-- src:9560 | (ii) another person who is able, by virtue of training or experience, to take, under the direction of a peace officer, samples of bodily substances from the person, by means of those investigative procedures.
@ref s 487.05(2) (src:9556-9560)
-- The judge "shall have regard to all relevant matters, including" the three named matters: a named matter is always one to have regard to;
-- another matter only if relevant; the text says nothing of an irrelevant one.
GIVEN matter IS A `s 487.05(2) matter the judge considers`
      `the matter is relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.05(2) the provincial court judge shall have regard to the matter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF matter EQUALS `s 487.05(2) another matter` AND `the matter is relevant` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF matter EQUALS `s 487.05(2) another matter` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- covers: 487.05(4)
-- fork: F14
-- jural: a peace officer > the person named in the warrant > power
-- src:9563 | (4) A warrant issued under subsection (1) may be executed at any place in Canada. Any peace officer who executes the warrant must have authority to act as a peace officer in the place where it is executed.
@ref s 487.05(4) (src:9563)
GIVEN `the place of execution is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer has authority to act as a peace officer in the place where the warrant is executed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.05(4) the warrant may be executed by the peace officer at the place` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the place of execution is in Canada` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF NOT `the peace officer has authority to act as a peace officer in the place where the warrant is executed` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must have authority to act as a peace officer in the place where it is executed"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 487.051 -- Order for samples of bodily substances: primary and secondary designated offences, persons found not criminally responsible`

DECLARE `s 487.051 how the person stands` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.051 convicted`
    `s 487.051 discharged under section 730`
    `s 487.051 found guilty under the Youth Criminal Justice Act`
    `s 487.051 found guilty under the Young Offenders Act`
    `s 487.051 found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder`
    `s 487.051 none of those`

-- covers: 487.051(1)
-- fork: F2
-- jural: the person convicted, discharged or found guilty > the court > liability
-- src:9565 | 487.051 (1) The court shall make an order in Form 5.03 authorizing the taking of the number of samples of bodily substances that is reasonably required for the purpose of forensic DNA analysis from a person who is convicted, discharged under section 730 or found guilty under the Youth Criminal Justice Act or the Young Offenders Act, of an offence committed at any time, including before June 30, 2000, if that offence is a primary designated offence within the meaning of paragraphs (a) and (c.02) of the definition primary designated offence in section 487.04 when the person is sentenced or discharged.
@ref s 487.051(1) (src:9565)
-- "shall make an order ... from a person who is convicted ... if that offence is a primary designated offence within the meaning of
-- paragraphs (a) and (c.02)": a duty. The persons named are a scope (NOTHING outside); the "if" is the text's own gate (JUST FALSE when the
-- offence is not within paragraphs (a) and (c.02): marginal reading (a)).
GIVEN `how the person stands` IS A `s 487.051 how the person stands`
      `s 487.04 the offence is a primary designated offence within paragraph (a) or (c.02) of the definition when the person is sentenced or discharged` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.051(1) the court shall make an order in Form 5.03` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `how the person stands` EQUALS `s 487.051 found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `how the person stands` EQUALS `s 487.051 none of those` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `s 487.04 the offence is a primary designated offence within paragraph (a) or (c.02) of the definition when the person is sentenced or discharged` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 487.04 the offence is a primary designated offence within paragraph (a) or (c.02) of the definition when the person is sentenced or discharged` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if that offence is a primary designated offence within the meaning of paragraphs (a) and (c.02) of the definition primary designated offence in section 487.04"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text)

-- covers: 487.051(2)
-- fork: F2
-- jural: the person convicted, discharged or found guilty > the court > liability
-- src:9567 | (2) The court shall make such an order in Form 5.03 in relation to a person who is convicted, discharged under section 730 or found guilty under the Youth Criminal Justice Act or the Young Offenders Act, of an offence committed at any time, including before June 30, 2000, if that offence is a primary designated offence within the meaning of any of paragraphs (a.1) to (c.01) and (c.03) to (d) of the definition primary designated offence in section 487.04 when the person is sentenced or discharged. However, the court is not required to make the order if it is satisfied that the person has established that the impact of such an order on their privacy and security of the person would be grossly disproportionate to the public interest in the protection of society and the proper administration of justice, to be achieved through the early detection, arrest and conviction of offenders.
@ref s 487.051(2) (src:9567)
GIVEN `how the person stands` IS A `s 487.051 how the person stands`
      `s 487.04 the offence is a primary designated offence within any of paragraphs (a.1) to (c.01) and (c.03) to (d) of the definition when the person is sentenced or discharged` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the person has established that the impact of such an order on their privacy and security of the person would be grossly disproportionate to the public interest in the protection of society and the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.051(2) the court shall make an order in Form 5.03` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `how the person stands` EQUALS `s 487.051 found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `how the person stands` EQUALS `s 487.051 none of those` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `s 487.04 the offence is a primary designated offence within any of paragraphs (a.1) to (c.01) and (c.03) to (d) of the definition when the person is sentenced or discharged` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if that offence is a primary designated offence within the meaning of any of paragraphs (a.1) to (c.01) and (c.03) to (d)"
        IF NOT (`s 487.04 the offence is a primary designated offence within any of paragraphs (a.1) to (c.01) and (c.03) to (d) of the definition when the person is sentenced or discharged` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text)
        IF `the court is satisfied that the person has established that the impact of such an order on their privacy and security of the person would be grossly disproportionate to the public interest in the protection of society and the proper administration of justice` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the court is not required to make the order if it is satisfied that the person has established that the impact of such an order"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- covers: 487.051(3), 487.051(3)(a), 487.051(3)(b), 487.051(3) closing words
-- fork: F1
-- jural: the court > the person found not criminally responsible, or convicted of a secondary designated offence > power
-- src:9569 | (3) The court may, on application by the prosecutor and if it is satisfied that it is in the best interests of the administration of justice to do so, make such an order in Form 5.04 in relation to
-- src:9570 | (a) a person who is found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for an offence committed at any time, including before June 30, 2000, if that offence is a designated offence when the finding is made; or
-- src:9571 | (b) a person who is convicted, discharged under section 730 or found guilty under the Youth Criminal Justice Act or the Young Offenders Act, of an offence committed at any time, including before June 30, 2000, if that offence is a secondary designated offence when the person is sentenced or discharged.
@ref s 487.051(3) (src:9569-9571)
-- The court MAY, on the prosecutor's application and if satisfied that it is in the best interests of the administration of justice, order
-- samples (Form 5.04) in the two cases (a) and (b). An "if" gate on a grant: a failed gate answers NOTHING (fork F1).
GIVEN `the prosecutor has applied for the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that it is in the best interests of the administration of justice to make the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `how the person stands` IS A `s 487.051 how the person stands`
      `s 487.04 the offence is a designated offence when the finding is made` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 487.04 the offence is a secondary designated offence when the person is sentenced or discharged` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.051(3) the court may make an order in Form 5.04` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the prosecutor has applied for the order` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF NOT `the court is satisfied that it is in the best interests of the administration of justice to make the order` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `how the person stands` EQUALS `s 487.051 found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` AND `s 487.04 the offence is a designated offence when the finding is made` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `how the person stands` EQUALS `s 487.051 convicted` AND `s 487.04 the offence is a secondary designated offence when the person is sentenced or discharged` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `how the person stands` EQUALS `s 487.051 discharged under section 730` AND `s 487.04 the offence is a secondary designated offence when the person is sentenced or discharged` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `how the person stands` EQUALS `s 487.051 found guilty under the Youth Criminal Justice Act` AND `s 487.04 the offence is a secondary designated offence when the person is sentenced or discharged` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `how the person stands` EQUALS `s 487.051 found guilty under the Young Offenders Act` AND `s 487.04 the offence is a secondary designated offence when the person is sentenced or discharged` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

DECLARE `s 487.051(3) matter the court considers` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.051(3) the person’s criminal record`
    `s 487.051(3) whether they were previously found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for a designated offence`
    `s 487.051(3) the nature of the offence`
    `s 487.051(3) the circumstances surrounding its commission`
    `s 487.051(3) the impact such an order would have on the person’s privacy and security of the person`
    `s 487.051(3) another matter`

-- covers: 487.051(3) closing words
-- jural: the person concerned > the court > right
-- src:9572 | In deciding whether to make the order, the court shall consider the person’s criminal record, whether they were previously found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for a designated offence, the nature of the offence, the circumstances surrounding its commission and the impact such an order would have on the person’s privacy and security of the person and shall give reasons for its decision.
@ref s 487.051(3) closing words (matters) (src:9572)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 487.051(3) matter the court considers`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.051(3) the court shall consider the matter in deciding whether to make the order` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `s 487.051(3) another matter` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed)
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 487.051(3) closing words (reasons) (src:9572)
GIVEN `the court is deciding whether to make the order in Form 5.04` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.051(3) the court shall give reasons for its decision` MEANS
    IF `the court is deciding whether to make the order in Form 5.04`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- covers: 487.051(4)
-- fork: G1
-- jural: the court > the person subject to the order > power
-- src:9574 | (4) When the court makes an order authorizing the taking of samples of bodily substances, it may make an order in Form 5.041 to require the person to report at the place, day and time set out in the order and submit to the taking of the samples.
@ref s 487.051(4) (src:9574)
-- "When the court makes an order authorizing the taking of samples ... it may make an order in Form 5.041": a "may" whose gate is "when".
-- Answered by the periods ruling (b) ("when" counts as "where": JUST FALSE when it fails); fork-register group G1, for a lawyer.
GIVEN `the court makes an order authorizing the taking of samples of bodily substances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.051(4) the court may make an order in Form 5.041 requiring the person to report and submit to the taking of the samples` MEANS
    IF `the court makes an order authorizing the taking of samples of bodily substances`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When the court makes an order authorizing the taking of samples of bodily substances"

§ `Section 487.053 -- Timing of order; hearing`

DECLARE `s 487.053(1) occasion` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.053(1) it imposes a sentence on a person`
    `s 487.053(1) it finds the person not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder`
    `s 487.053(1) it directs that they be discharged under section 730`
    `s 487.053(1) another occasion`

-- covers: 487.053(1)
-- fork: G1
-- jural: the court > the person to be sentenced, found not criminally responsible or discharged > power
-- src:9577 | 487.053 (1) The court may make an order under section 487.051 authorizing the taking of samples of bodily substances when it imposes a sentence on a person, finds the person not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or directs that they be discharged under section 730.
@ref s 487.053(1) (src:9577)
GIVEN occasion IS A `s 487.053(1) occasion`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.053(1) the court may make an order under section 487.051 at this time` MEANS
    CONSIDER occasion
    WHEN `s 487.053(1) another occasion` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when it imposes a sentence on a person, finds the person not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or directs that they be discharged under section 730"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- covers: 487.053(2), 487.053(2)(a)
-- jural: the person concerned > the court > right
-- src:9579 | (2) If the court does not consider the matter at that time, it
-- src:9580 | (a) shall, within 90 days after the day on which it imposes the sentence, makes the finding or directs that the person be discharged, set a date for a hearing to do so;
-- src:9581 | (b) retains jurisdiction over the matter; and
-- src:9582 | (c) may require the person to appear by closed-circuit television or videoconference, as long as the person is given the opportunity to communicate privately with counsel if they are represented by counsel.
@ref s 487.053(2) (src:9579-9582)
-- "If the court does not consider the matter at that time, it (a) shall, within 90 days ... set a date for a hearing; (b) retains jurisdiction; (c) may require
-- the person to appear by closed-circuit television or videoconference, as long as ...". (a) and (b) are duties gated by "If" (JUST FALSE when it fails: marginal
-- reading (a)); (c) is a grant gated by "If" (NOTHING: fork F1) and by "as long as" (JUST FALSE).
GIVEN `the court did not consider the matter at the time of the sentence, the finding or the discharge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.053(2)(a) the court shall set a date for a hearing within 90 days` MEANS
    IF `the court did not consider the matter at the time of the sentence, the finding or the discharge`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the court does not consider the matter at that time"

-- covers: 487.053(2)(b)
-- jural: the person concerned > the court > right
@ref s 487.053(2)(b) (src:9579-9581)
GIVEN `the court did not consider the matter at the time of the sentence, the finding or the discharge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.053(2)(b) the court retains jurisdiction over the matter` MEANS
    IF `the court did not consider the matter at the time of the sentence, the finding or the discharge`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the court does not consider the matter at that time"

-- covers: 487.053(2)(c)
-- fork: G1,F1
-- jural: the court > the person concerned > power
@ref s 487.053(2)(c) (src:9579-9582)
GIVEN `the court did not consider the matter at the time of the sentence, the finding or the discharge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is given the opportunity to communicate privately with counsel if they are represented by counsel` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.053(2)(c) the court may require the person to appear by closed-circuit television or videoconference` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court did not consider the matter at the time of the sentence, the finding or the discharge` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF NOT `the person is given the opportunity to communicate privately with counsel if they are represented by counsel` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "as long as the person is given the opportunity to communicate privately with counsel if they are represented by counsel"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The 90 days of paragraph (a), as a period: the last day on which the court may set the date. "within 90 days after the day on which it imposes the
-- sentence, makes the finding or directs that the person be discharged": that day plus 90 days.
@ref s 487.053(2)(a) (the period) (src:9579-9580)
GIVEN `the day on which the court imposes the sentence, makes the finding or directs that the person be discharged` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 487.053(2)(a) the last day for the court to set a date for the hearing` MEANS
    `the day on which the court imposes the sentence, makes the finding or directs that the person be discharged` PLUS 90

GIVEN `the day on which the court imposes the sentence, makes the finding or directs that the person be discharged` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the court sets the date for the hearing` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 487.053(2)(a) the court set the date within 90 days` MEANS
    `the day on which the court sets the date for the hearing` AT MOST `s 487.053(2)(a) the last day for the court to set a date for the hearing` `the day on which the court imposes the sentence, makes the finding or directs that the person be discharged`

DECLARE `s 487.053(2)(a) action` IS ONE OF `s 487.053(2)(a) set a date for a hearing`

-- The duty as a regulative rule: the court MUST set a date for a hearing WITHIN 90 (days, counted from the day of the sentence, finding or discharge).
-- The text states no consequence of missing the 90 days; the LEST is therefore a bare BREACH naming the court (nothing is invented). #TRACE is read, not asserted.
@ref s 487.053(2)(a) (the duty) (src:9579-9580)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 487.053(2)(a) action`
`s 487.053(2)(a) the court must set a date for the hearing` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 487.053(2)(a) set a date for a hearing`
    WITHIN 90
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "no date was set for the hearing within 90 days after the sentence, the finding or the direction to discharge"


§ `Section 487.054 -- Appeal`

DECLARE `s 487.054 appellant` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.054 the offender`
    `s 487.054 the prosecutor`
    `s 487.054 someone else`

DECLARE `s 487.054 decision` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.054 a decision under subsection 487.051(1)`
    `s 487.054 a decision under subsection 487.051(2)`
    `s 487.054 a decision under subsection 487.051(3)`
    `s 487.054 another decision`

-- covers: 487.054
-- jural: the offender or the prosecutor > the court of appeal > power
-- src:9584 | 487.054 The offender or the prosecutor may appeal from a decision of the court under any of subsections 487.051(1) to (3).
@ref s 487.054 (src:9584)
GIVEN appellant IS A `s 487.054 appellant`
      decision IS A `s 487.054 decision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.054 the person may appeal from the decision of the court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF appellant EQUALS `s 487.054 someone else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF decision EQUALS `s 487.054 another decision` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

