-- covers: 487.055(3), 487.055(3)(a.1), 487.055(3)(d)
-- jural: none
-- src:9595 | Definition of sexual offence
-- src:9596 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (1), sexual offence means
-- src:9597 | (a) an offence under any of the following provisions, namely,
-- src:9598 | (i) section 151 (sexual interference),
-- src:9599 | (ii) section 152 (invitation to sexual touching or exposure),
-- src:9600 | (iii) section 153 (sexual exploitation),
-- src:9601 | (iv) section 155 (incest),
-- src:9602 | (v) subsection 212(4) (offence in relation to juvenile prostitution),
-- src:9603 | (vi) section 271 (sexual assault),
-- src:9604 | (vii) section 272 (sexual assault with a weapon, threats to a third party or causing bodily harm), and
-- src:9605 | (viii) section 273 (aggravated sexual assault);
-- src:9606 | (a.1) an offence under subsection 348(1) if the indictable offence referred to in that subsection is a sexual offence within the meaning of paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d);
-- src:9607 | (b) an offence under any of the following provisions of the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as they read from time to time before January 4, 1983, namely,
-- src:9608 | (i) section 144 (rape),
-- src:9609 | (ii) section 146 (sexual intercourse with female under fourteen or between fourteen and sixteen),
-- src:9610 | (iii) section 148 (sexual intercourse with feeble-minded, etc.),
-- src:9611 | (iv) section 149 (indecent assault on female),
-- src:9612 | (v) section 156 (indecent assault on male), or
-- src:9613 | (vi) section 157 (acts of gross indecency);
-- src:9614 | (c) an offence under paragraph 153(1)(a) (sexual intercourse with step-daughter, etc.) of the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as it read from time to time before January 1, 1988; and
-- src:9615 | (d) an attempt to commit an offence referred to in any of paragraphs (a) to (c).
@ref s 487.055(3) (src:9595-9615)
-- "sexual offence means": a closed definition, so a provision outside the four limbs is JUST FALSE. Paragraph (a.1): section 348(1) when the indictable offence
-- it refers to is itself a sexual offence within paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d). Paragraph (d): an attempt to commit an offence referred to in (a) to (c).
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `s 487.055(3) offence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.055(3) the offence is a sexual offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the offence`'s `it is an attempt to commit that offence` AND `s 487.055(3) the offence attempted is one referred to in paragraphs (a) to (c)` `the offence` THEN JUST TRUE   -- paragraph (d)
        IF `the offence`'s `it is an attempt to commit that offence` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "sexual offence means"
        IF `the offence`'s `enactment` EQUALS `s 487.055(3) this Act` AND elem (`the offence`'s `provision`) `s 487.055(3)(a) the provisions` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the offence`'s `enactment` EQUALS `s 487.055(3) this Act` AND (`the offence`'s `provision`) EQUALS (`Provision of the Code` OF 348, "(1)") AND `the offence`'s `the indictable offence referred to in subsection 348(1) is itself a sexual offence within the meaning of paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d)` THEN JUST TRUE   -- paragraph (a.1)
        IF `the offence`'s `enactment` EQUALS `s 487.055(3) the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as it read from time to time before January 4, 1983` AND elem (`the offence`'s `provision`) `s 487.055(3)(b) the provisions` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the offence`'s `enactment` EQUALS `s 487.055(3) the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as it read from time to time before January 1, 1988` AND (`the offence`'s `provision`) EQUALS `s 487.055(3)(c) the provision` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "sexual offence means"

-- Paragraph (d) reaches an attempt to commit an offence referred to in (a) to (c): the same test, applied to the offence attempted.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `s 487.055(3) offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 487.055(3) the offence attempted is one referred to in paragraphs (a) to (c)` MEANS
        (`the offence`'s `enactment` EQUALS `s 487.055(3) this Act` AND elem (`the offence`'s `provision`) `s 487.055(3)(a) the provisions`)
    OR  (`the offence`'s `enactment` EQUALS `s 487.055(3) this Act` AND (`the offence`'s `provision`) EQUALS (`Provision of the Code` OF 348, "(1)") AND `the offence`'s `the indictable offence referred to in subsection 348(1) is itself a sexual offence within the meaning of paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d)`)
    OR  (`the offence`'s `enactment` EQUALS `s 487.055(3) the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as it read from time to time before January 4, 1983` AND elem (`the offence`'s `provision`) `s 487.055(3)(b) the provisions`)
    OR  (`the offence`'s `enactment` EQUALS `s 487.055(3) the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as it read from time to time before January 1, 1988` AND (`the offence`'s `provision`) EQUALS `s 487.055(3)(c) the provision`)

DECLARE `s 487.055(1) basis` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.055(1)(a) had been declared a dangerous offender under Part XXIV`
    `s 487.055(1)(b) had been declared a dangerous offender or a dangerous sexual offender under Part XXI of the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as it read from time to time before January 1, 1988`
    `s 487.055(1)(c) had been convicted of murder`
    `s 487.055(1)(c.1) had been convicted of attempted murder or conspiracy to commit murder or to cause another person to be murdered`
    `s 487.055(1)(d) had been convicted of a sexual offence within the meaning of subsection (3)`
    `s 487.055(1)(e) had been convicted of manslaughter`
    `s 487.055(1) none of those`

-- covers: 487.055(1), 487.055(1)(a), 487.055(1)(b), 487.055(1)(c), 487.055(1)(c.1), 487.055(1)(d), 487.055(1)(e)
-- fork: F1
-- jural: a provincial court judge > a person who, before June 30, 2000, had been declared a dangerous offender or convicted of murder, manslaughter or a sexual offence > power
-- src:9586 | 487.055 (1) A provincial court judge may, on ex parte application made in Form 5.05, authorize in Form 5.06 the taking, for the purpose of forensic DNA analysis, of any number of samples of bodily substances that is reasonably required for that purpose, by means of the investigative procedures described in subsection 487.06(1), from a person who, before June 30, 2000,
-- src:9587 | (a) had been declared a dangerous offender under Part XXIV;
-- src:9588 | (b) had been declared a dangerous offender or a dangerous sexual offender under Part XXI of the Criminal Code, being chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as it read from time to time before January 1, 1988;
-- src:9589 | (c) had been convicted of murder;
-- src:9590 | (c.1) had been convicted of attempted murder or conspiracy to commit murder or to cause another person to be murdered and, on the date of the application, is serving a sentence of imprisonment for that offence;
-- src:9591 | (d) had been convicted of a sexual offence within the meaning of subsection (3) and, on the date of the application, is serving a sentence of imprisonment for that offence; or
-- src:9592 | (e) had been convicted of manslaughter and, on the date of the application, is serving a sentence of imprisonment for that offence.
@ref s 487.055(1) (src:9586-9592)
-- A provincial court judge MAY, on ex parte application in Form 5.05, authorize in Form 5.06 the taking of samples from a person who, before June 30, 2000, fell
-- within one of (a) to (e); (c.1), (d) and (e) also need the person to be serving a sentence of imprisonment for that offence on the date of the application.
GIVEN `the application is made ex parte in Form 5.05` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the event happened before June 30, 2000` IS A BOOLEAN
      basis IS A `s 487.055(1) basis`
      `s 487.055(3) the offence is a sexual offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `on the date of the application the person is serving a sentence of imprisonment for that offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.055(1) the provincial court judge may authorize in Form 5.06 the taking of samples of bodily substances` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the application is made ex parte in Form 5.05` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF NOT `the event happened before June 30, 2000` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF basis EQUALS `s 487.055(1)(a) had been declared a dangerous offender under Part XXIV` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF basis EQUALS `s 487.055(1)(b) had been declared a dangerous offender or a dangerous sexual offender under Part XXI of the Criminal Code, chapter C-34 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as it read from time to time before January 1, 1988` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF basis EQUALS `s 487.055(1)(c) had been convicted of murder` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF basis EQUALS `s 487.055(1)(c.1) had been convicted of attempted murder or conspiracy to commit murder or to cause another person to be murdered` AND `on the date of the application the person is serving a sentence of imprisonment for that offence` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF basis EQUALS `s 487.055(1)(d) had been convicted of a sexual offence within the meaning of subsection (3)` AND `s 487.055(3) the offence is a sexual offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `on the date of the application the person is serving a sentence of imprisonment for that offence` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF basis EQUALS `s 487.055(1)(e) had been convicted of manslaughter` AND `on the date of the application the person is serving a sentence of imprisonment for that offence` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- covers: 487.055(2)
-- jural: the person concerned > the applicant > right
-- src:9594 | (2) The application shall be accompanied by a certificate referred to in paragraph 667(1)(a) that establishes that the person is a person referred to in subsection (1). The certificate may be received in evidence without giving the notice referred to in subsection 667(4).
@ref s 487.055(2) (the certificate accompanies the application) (src:9594)
