      `the certificate establishes that the person is a person referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.055(2) the application is accompanied by the certificate` MEANS
    IF `a certificate referred to in paragraph 667(1)(a) accompanies the application` AND `the certificate establishes that the person is a person referred to in subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The application shall be accompanied by a certificate referred to in paragraph 667(1)(a) that establishes that the person is a person referred to in subsection (1)."

@ref s 487.055(2) (the certificate in evidence) (src:9594)
GIVEN `a certificate referred to in paragraph 667(1)(a) accompanies the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.055(2) the certificate may be received in evidence without the notice referred to in subsection 667(4)` MEANS
    IF `a certificate referred to in paragraph 667(1)(a) accompanies the application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- covers: 487.055(3.01)
