      `the person wishes to appear at the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is given the opportunity to communicate privately with counsel if they are represented by counsel` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.055(3.01) the court may require the person to appear by closed-circuit television or videoconference` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is given notice of an application under subsection (1)` AND `the person wishes to appear at the hearing`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF NOT `the person is given the opportunity to communicate privately with counsel if they are represented by counsel` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "as long as the person is given the opportunity to communicate privately with counsel if they are represented by counsel"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

