`s 487.055(4) a summons in Form 5.061 shall be directed to the person requiring them to report and submit to the taking of the samples` MEANS
    IF `the person is on conditional release` AND `the person has not appeared at the hearing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if a person who is on conditional release has not appeared at the hearing"

DECLARE `s 487.055(5) how the summons is served` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.055(5) delivered personally to the person to whom it is directed`
    `s 487.055(5) left at the person’s latest or usual place of residence with a person found there`
    `s 487.055(5) served in another way`

-- covers: 487.055(5)
-- jural: the person to be served > a peace officer > right
-- src:9625 | (5) The summons shall be accompanied by a copy of the authorization referred to in subsection (1) and be served by a peace officer who shall either deliver it personally to the person to whom it is directed or, if that person cannot conveniently be found, leave it for the person at their latest or usual place of residence with any person found there who appears to be at least sixteen years of age.
@ref s 487.055(5) (src:9625)
GIVEN `the summons is accompanied by a copy of the authorization` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the summons is served by a peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      how IS A `s 487.055(5) how the summons is served`
      `the person to whom it is directed cannot conveniently be found` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person found there appears to be at least sixteen years of age` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.055(5) the summons is served as the subsection requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the summons is accompanied by a copy of the authorization` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The summons shall be accompanied by a copy of the authorization"
        IF NOT `the summons is served by a peace officer` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "be served by a peace officer who shall either deliver it personally"
        IF how EQUALS `s 487.055(5) delivered personally to the person to whom it is directed` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF how EQUALS `s 487.055(5) left at the person’s latest or usual place of residence with a person found there` AND `the person to whom it is directed cannot conveniently be found` AND `the person found there appears to be at least sixteen years of age` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall either deliver it personally to the person to whom it is directed or, if that person cannot conveniently be found, leave it for the person at their latest or usual place of residence with any person found there who appears to be at least sixteen years of age"

§ `Section 487.0551 -- Failure to appear`

DECLARE `s 487.0551(1) document not appeared at` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.0551(1) an order made under subsection 487.051(4)`
    `s 487.0551(1) an order made under subsection 487.055(3.11)`
    `s 487.0551(1) a summons referred to in subsection 487.055(4)`
    `s 487.0551(1) a summons referred to in subsection 487.091(3)`
    `s 487.0551(1) another document`

-- covers: 487.0551(1)
-- fork: F1
-- jural: a justice of the peace > the person who failed to appear > power
-- src:9629 | 487.0551 (1) If a person fails to appear at the place, day and time set out in an order made under subsection 487.051(4) or 487.055(3.11) or in a summons referred to in subsection 487.055(4) or 487.091(3), a justice of the peace may issue a warrant for their arrest in Form 5.062 to allow samples of bodily substances to be taken.
@ref s 487.0551(1) (src:9629)
GIVEN document IS A `s 487.0551(1) document not appeared at`
      `the person fails to appear at the place, day and time set out in it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0551(1) a justice of the peace may issue a warrant for the arrest of the person in Form 5.062` MEANS
    IF document EQUALS `s 487.0551(1) another document`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
    ELSE IF `the person fails to appear at the place, day and time set out in it`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- covers: 487.0551(2)
-- jural: a peace officer > the person named in the warrant > power
-- src:9631 | (2) The warrant may be executed anywhere in Canada by a peace officer who has jurisdiction in that place or over the person. The warrant remains in force until it is executed.
@ref s 487.0551(2) (src:9631)
GIVEN `the place is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer has jurisdiction in that place or over the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0551(2) the warrant may be executed by the peace officer at the place` MEANS
    IF `the place is in Canada` AND `the peace officer has jurisdiction in that place or over the person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

@ref s 487.0551(2) (in force until executed) (src:9631)
GIVEN `the warrant has been executed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0551(2) the warrant remains in force` MEANS
    IF `the warrant has been executed`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The warrant remains in force until it is executed."
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 487.0552 -- Failure to comply with order or summons`

DECLARE `s 487.0552(1) order or summons` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.0552(1) an order made under subsection 487.051(4) of this Act`
    `s 487.0552(1) an order made under subsection 487.055(3.11) of this Act`
    `s 487.0552(1) an order made under subsection 196.14(4) of the National Defence Act`
    `s 487.0552(1) an order made under subsection 196.24(4) of the National Defence Act`
    `s 487.0552(1) a summons referred to in subsection 487.055(4) of this Act`
    `s 487.0552(1) a summons referred to in subsection 487.091(3) of this Act`
    `s 487.0552(1) another document`

-- covers: 487.0552(1), 487.0552(1)(a), 487.0552(1)(b)
-- jural: the state > the person who fails to comply > power
-- src:9633 | 487.0552 (1) Every person who, without reasonable excuse, fails to comply with an order made under subsection 487.051(4) or 487.055(3.11) of this Act or under subsection 196.14(4) or 196.24(4) of the National Defence Act, or with a summons referred to in subsection 487.055(4) or 487.091(3) of this Act, is guilty of
-- src:9634 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or
-- src:9635 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 487.0552(1) (src:9633-9635)
-- "Every person who, without reasonable excuse, fails to comply ... is guilty of": an offence. "without reasonable excuse" limits the offence in its own words, so
-- a person with a reasonable excuse, a person who complied, and a document the section does not name fall outside it: NOTHING. Limb (b) is "an offence punishable on
-- summary conviction" and states no penalty (section 787, outside these sources, does).
GIVEN document IS A `s 487.0552(1) order or summons`
      `the person fails to comply with it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0552(1) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF document EQUALS `s 487.0552(1) another document` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF NOT `the person fails to comply with it` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `the person has a reasonable excuse` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 487.0552(1) (the punishments) (src:9633-9635)
`s 487.0552(1) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`
    Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- covers: 487.0552(2)
-- fork: F3
-- jural: a person subject to the Code of Service Discipline > the court > immunity
-- src:9637 | (2) For greater certainty, a lawful command that prevents a person from complying with an order or summons is a reasonable excuse if, at the time, the person is subject to the Code of Service Discipline within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the National Defence Act.
@ref s 487.0552(2) (src:9637)
GIVEN `a lawful command prevents the person from complying with the order or summons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time the person is subject to the Code of Service Discipline within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the National Defence Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0552(2) a lawful command that prevents the person from complying is a reasonable excuse` MEANS
    IF `a lawful command prevents the person from complying with the order or summons` AND `at the time the person is subject to the Code of Service Discipline within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the National Defence Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is a reasonable excuse if, at the time, the person is subject to the Code of Service Discipline"
